ps:\/\/wp.me\/p8u1BN-72","jetpack-related-posts":[{"id":554,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/12\/25\/dancers-part-4\/","url_meta":{"origin":436,"position":0},"title":"Dancers &#8211; part 4","date":"December 25, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"We met again for a final rehearsal before our first concert. Despite what I stated in the previous post, We agreed on that we had reached a state where we temporarily are agreeing on the expression of the concept and should for a while just improvise together without any specific\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/p554.jpg?fit=1200%2C675&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":401,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/11\/01\/dancers\/","url_meta":{"origin":436,"position":1},"title":"Dancers","date":"November 1, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"As stated in my project description: - Look at the possibilities for at external sources, such as the audience, a net stream, dancers, humidity, lights etc. can control the development in the music and in the video trough out a performance by using alternative sensors, controllers and programs. I want\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/p401.jpg?fit=1200%2C675&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":1253,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2012\/06\/07\/exploring-improvisation-techniques-with-dance-drums-and-electronics\/","url_meta":{"origin":436,"position":2},"title":"Exploring improvisation techniques with dance, drums and electronics","date":"June 7, 2012","format":false,"excerpt":"What: An analysis and discussion of a rehearsal where we explored some improvisation techniques. Why: To see the exercises from the outside and experience their expression. How: I will analyze and discuss each exercise and explain how we prepared and conducted them. -------- Preface: In March of this year we\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2012\/06\/helenarosenlund_jonashedvig_0152.jpg?fit=1200%2C797&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":5,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/hello-world-2\/","url_meta":{"origin":436,"position":3},"title":"Hello World!","date":"September 13, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"In this blog, I\u2019ll explain and reflect upon my approach to the combination of drums and electronics, my current setup and some thoughts regarding the form of my performances. The blog will run for a minimum of two years as a documentation of the process in my master degree at\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/1.jpg?w=350&h=200&crop=1","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":749,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2012\/01\/15\/dancer-controlling-sound-with-sensors-idea-sketch\/","url_meta":{"origin":436,"position":4},"title":"Dancer controlling sound with sensors &#8211; Idea sketch","date":"January 15, 2012","format":false,"excerpt":"(...) a sensor based setup for a dancer and a drummer, where the dancer can pick up sounds played by the drummer and process them with movement (...) My project description What: Dancer wearing sensors - controlling sound. The idea is that the dancer can approach my drum set (sound\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2012\/01\/lydplukking-e1368445521324.jpg?fit=896%2C1200&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":14,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/why\/","url_meta":{"origin":436,"position":5},"title":"Why?","date":"September 13, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"So, why am I doing this? I\u2019ve always been jealous at the guitarists ability to just go and buy an effect pedal, send the sound of his guitar trough it and control it with his feet. I want to do the same thing, just that my instrument is a drum\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/2.jpg?w=350&h=200&crop=1","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]}],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/436"}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=436"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/436\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1905,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/436\/revisions\/1905"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1668"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=436"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=436"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=436"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}